{"id":184,"name":"azumarill","speciesId":184,"dex":184,"form":"normal","generation":2,"types":["water","fairy"],"stats":{"hp":100,"attack":50,"defense":80,"special-attack":60,"special-defense":80,"speed":50},"abilities":[{"name":"thick-fat","hidden":false},{"name":"huge-power","hidden":false},{"name":"sap-sipper","hidden":true}],"height":8,"weight":285,"baseExp":189,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/184.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/184.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/184.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/184.ogg","genus":"Aqua Rabbit Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"emerald","text":"It lives in water virtually all day long. Its body color and pattern act as camouflage that makes it tough for enemies to spot in water."},{"version":"gold","text":"By keeping still and listening in­ tently, it can tell what is in even wild, fast- moving rivers."},{"version":"silver","text":"When it plays in water, it rolls up its elongated ears to prevent their insides from get­ ting wet."},{"version":"crystal","text":"The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it's in the water."},{"version":"ruby","text":"AZUMARILL’s long ears are indispensable sensors. By focusing its hearing, this POKéMON can identify what kinds of prey are around, even in rough and fast-running rivers."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"AZUMARILL can make balloons out of air. It makes these air balloons if it spots a drowning POKéMON. The air balloons enable the POKéMON in trouble to breathe."},{"version":"firered","text":"When it plays in water, it rolls up its elongated ears to prevent their insides from getting wet."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"By keeping still and listening intently, it can even tell what is in wild, fast-moving rivers."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It lives in rivers and lakes. In water, its coloring and patterns trick the vision of foes."},{"version":"pearl","text":"Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of living things on riverbeds."},{"version":"platinum","text":"It can spend all day in water, since it can inhale and store a large volume of air."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"By keeping still and listening intently, it can tell what is in even wild, fast-moving rivers."},{"version":"black-2","text":"Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of things in water and tell what they are."},{"version":"y","text":"The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it’s in the water."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Azumarill’s long ears are indispensable sensors. By focusing its hearing, this Pokémon can identify what kinds of prey are around, even in rough and fast-running rivers."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Azumarill can make balloons out of air. It makes these air balloons if it spots a drowning Pokémon. The air balloons enable the Pokémon in trouble to breathe."},{"version":"sword","text":"It spends most of its time in the water. On sunny days, Azumarill floats on the surface of the water and sunbathes."},{"version":"shield","text":"These Pokémon create air-filled bubbles. When Azurill play in rivers, Azumarill will cover them with these bubbles."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":75,"eggGroups":["water1","fairy"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"azurill","speciesId":298,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Felicidade alta"],"species":"marill","speciesId":183,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 18"],"species":"azumarill","speciesId":184,"evolvesTo":[]}]}]},"varieties":[{"id":184,"name":"azumarill","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/184.png"}],"games":[3,4,5,6,7,8,9,1